Subject: [PATCH] ARM: skip PSCI DT fixup in V851S SPL OS boot

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [proof of concept]

The ARMv7 SPL FIT path does not link armv7_boot_nonsec() from bootm.c.
V851S SPL also enters Linux directly without installing a PSCI monitor.
Skip the PSCI DT fixup in V851S SPL; U-Boot proper retains its boot-mode
check and PSCI fixup. FEL-loaded SPI-NAND staging selects NAND through the
sunxi SPL boot-device choice introduced earlier in this series.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm/cpu/armv7/virt-dt.c b/arch/arm/cpu/armv7/virt-dt.c
index 5dc7ed5e27..1f3c6d61c8 100644
--- a/arch/arm/cpu/armv7/virt-dt.c
+++ b/arch/arm/cpu/armv7/virt-dt.c
@@ -55,7 +55,12 @@ int armv7_apply_memory_carveout(u64 *start, u64 *size)
 
 int psci_update_dt(void *fdt)
 {
+	/* V851S SPL jumps directly to Linux without a resident monitor. */
+#if defined(CONFIG_MACH_SUN8I_V851S) && defined(CONFIG_XPL_BUILD)
+	return 0;
+#endif
+
-#ifdef CONFIG_ARMV7_NONSEC
+#if defined(CONFIG_ARMV7_NONSEC) && !defined(CONFIG_XPL_BUILD)
 	if (!armv7_boot_nonsec())
 		return 0;
 #endif
